            "Hi everyone, thanks for coming to this short session on managing money at university. I know budgeting sounds boring, but trust me, it's much less boring than running out of money in the middle of the month. So, first things first. As soon as your grant or wages arrive, move a small amount into a separate savings account. Even a tenth makes a real difference. Treat that money as if it doesn't exist. Next, look at your fixed costs, things like rent, transport and your phone. These are the same every month, so take them away first. What's left is what you can actually spend on food, going out and everything else. Divide that by four, and you've got a weekly limit. Many students I talk to say their biggest problem isn't rent. It's small daily spending, like coffee on the way to lectures or ordering food late at night. So try cooking in batches on Sundays. It's cheaper and healthier. And finally, don't be embarrassed to use student discounts. Always ask. You'd be amazed how many shops, cinemas and museums offer them.",
