        new("l-b2-3", "B2", new ComprehensionExercise(
            "The Long Road to the Zip",
            "Here's a question for you. What do jackets, bags and tents all have in common? The zip, of course. It's so ordinary that we never think about it. But it took inventors several decades to get it right. In the eighteen nineties, an American inventor called Whitcomb Judson showed a device for fastening shoes. It used hooks and eyes, and it was clever, but it often got stuck or came open by itself. People weren't impressed. Then, in nineteen thirteen, a Swedish engineer working in America, Gideon Sundback, designed a much better version. Instead of hooks, it had small teeth that locked together neatly, and it was far more reliable. Even so, the invention was slow to catch on. At first, it was mainly used for boots and tobacco pouches. The name zipper actually came from a company that made rubber boots, because of the sound the fastener made. It was only in the nineteen thirties, when fashion designers began putting zips into trousers and children's clothes, that the zip truly became part of everyday life.",
            [
                new("What is the talk mainly about?", ["Judson's device was an immediate success", "The zip took a long time to develop and become popular", "The zip was first designed for trousers", "Rubber boots were invented in Sweden"], 1, "The speaker says \"it took inventors several decades to get it right\" and that it \"was slow to catch on\"."),
                new("What was the problem with Judson's device?", ["It often got stuck or came open by itself", "It was too expensive to make", "It was too heavy to wear", "It only worked on bags"], 0, "The speaker says \"it often got stuck or came open by itself\"."),
                new("Where did the name zipper come from?", ["A famous fashion designer", "The inventor's surname", "A Swedish word for teeth", "A company that made rubber boots"], 3, "The speaker says, \"The name zipper actually came from a company that made rubber boots.\""),
                new("When did the zip truly become part of everyday life?", ["In the eighteen nineties", "In nineteen thirteen", "In the nineteen thirties", "In the nineteen fifties"], 2, "The speaker says \"it was only in the nineteen thirties\" that the zip \"truly became part of everyday life\"."),
            ])),
