            "A Manager's Advice on Remote Work",
            "Hello, and thanks for tuning in to Work Smart. A listener asked me what I've learned from managing a team that works almost entirely from home. So here are my three lessons. The first is about boundaries. When your office is also your kitchen, work can easily take over your whole day. I encourage my team to have a clear finishing time and, if possible, a separate space for work, even if it's just a small desk in a corner. The second lesson is about communication. In an office, you notice when a colleague looks stressed. Online, you don't. So I have a short video call with each person every week, and it's not about tasks. It's simply to ask how they're doing. The third lesson surprised me. People who work from home often feel they have to prove they're busy, so they answer messages instantly, even late at night. I tell my team clearly that I judge results, not reply times. Since I started saying that, people seem calmer, and honestly, the quality of their work has improved.",
