        new("l-b2-6", "B2", new ComprehensionExercise(
            "A Potter on Learning Patience",
            "People often ask me what pottery has taught me, and my answer is always the same. Patience. Not skill, not creativity, but patience. When I started, I was twenty-five and I was used to getting results quickly. At work, I sent an email and got an answer in minutes. Clay doesn't work like that. My first teacher made me practise centring the clay on the wheel for a whole month before I was allowed to make a single bowl. I was furious. I thought she was wasting my time. But she was right. If the clay isn't perfectly centred, everything you build on top of it will wobble and eventually collapse. Then there's the drying, which can take a week, and the firing in the kiln, which can crack a piece you've spent days on. You learn to accept that some work will fail. Oddly enough, that lesson has made me calmer in the rest of my life too. When something goes wrong now, I simply start again.",
            [
                new("What is the speaker's main message?", ["Pottery is a good way to earn money", "Pottery taught the speaker to be patient", "Teachers should not be too strict", "Clay is difficult to buy"], 1, "The speaker says, \"People often ask me what pottery has taught me, and my answer is always the same. Patience.\""),
                new("How did the speaker feel about practising centring for a month?", ["Grateful", "Bored but calm", "Proud", "Furious"], 3, "The speaker says, \"I was furious. I thought she was wasting my time.\""),
                new("What happens if the clay isn't centred?", ["What you build will wobble and collapse", "It dries too quickly", "It changes colour in the kiln", "It becomes too heavy to lift"], 0, "The speaker says, \"Everything you build on top of it will wobble and eventually collapse.\""),
                new("How has pottery changed the speaker's life outside the studio?", ["The speaker now works faster", "The speaker has stopped using email", "The speaker is calmer when things go wrong", "The speaker has become a teacher"], 2, "The speaker says, \"That lesson has made me calmer in the rest of my life too.\""),
